  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing The Server**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in building `/server/auth.ts`, focusing on JWT creation, verification, role-based middleware, and robust password validation. Simultaneously, I\'m meticulously designing `/server.ts`, ensuring a complete Express REST API with the necessary Vite middleware and static serving for production. I\'m carefully reviewing all the API endpoints.\n\n\n**Defining API Endpoints**\n\nI\'ve just added API endpoints to the existing `/server.ts` file. I\'m focusing on defining the `/api/health` health check. For the authentication features, I have defined these endpoints: `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me`, `PUT /api/auth/profile`, and `POST /api/auth/switch-activity`. I\'m now turning my attention to Geo and Routing.\n\n\n**Defining New API Routes**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new API routes. I\'ve designed `/api/geo` endpoints: `GET /api/geo/reverse` for reverse geocoding, and `POST /api/geo/route` to provide route details.\n\nNext up, I\'m setting up the pricing routes with `/api/pricing/configs` and `/api/pricing/calculate`. I am also working on MOVEX Guard and Intelligence, defining `/api/intelligence/guard-check` and `/api/intelligence/match`. Finally, the bookings and tracking with FinTech are underway with `POST /api/bookings`. I am ensuring that prohibited bookings are rejected with a security alert.\n\n\n**Refining Booking Features**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the `/api/bookings` endpoints! I\'m adding `security_alerts` records for Admin review when appropriate, handling both specific partner/journey selection or broadcast options for bookings. I\'m also ensuring clean base64/uploaded parcel photo handling. Furthermore, I\'ve defined endpoints for listing sender bookings and fetching single bookings by ID or `parcel_code`, including tracking, payment, and alerts. Finally, I\'m working on payment simulation and status updates with `/api/bookings/:id/pay`.\n\n\n**Expanding Booking Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing `/api/bookings/:id/cancel`, including simulated cancellation fee calculation and refund records. I\'ve also implemented `/api/bookings/:id/meeting-point` for sender/partner pickup and dropoff agreement. `/api/bookings/:id/dispute` is in progress; this will raise a dispute, update the status to `DISPUTED` and set payment to `ON_HOLD`. Furthermore, I\'ve defined the partner journeys and requests endpoints, starting with the overview and journeys listings. I\'m focusing on defining POST, PATCH and DELETE endpoints for partner journeys. Finally, the requests endpoint is underway.\n\n\n**Implementing Partner Routes**\n\nI\'m now focused on atomic transactions for `/api/partner/requests/:id/accept`, ensuring partner assignments are exclusive using SQLite\'s transaction features. If another partner accepted first, I will be returning a 409 conflict. I\'m also implementing the rejection endpoint, `/api/partner/requests/:id/reject`, recording rejections to hide them for the partner. I\'ve started the implementation of `/api/partner/deliveries` routes, starting with the active and completed deliveries, including pickup verification, handover, and GPS simulation. I\'m focusing on `/api/partner/deliveries/:id/handover` next.\n\n\n**Defining Admin APIs**\n\nI am now structuring the Admin Dashboard API endpoints, applying the `requireRole(\'admin\')` middleware for strict access control. I\'m focused on the `/api/admin/deliveries/:id/deliver-otp` endpoint, which verifies the `delivery_otp` and transitions the delivery status to `DELIVERED`, while also updating partner statistics and recalculating their reliability score. I\'ve been structuring the Admin-specific routes for overall KPIs with Recharts analytics, user management with status updates, bookings listings, Guard alerts with decision-making capabilities, and comprehensive payment data display.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_10718443886967845404"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import jwt from \'jsonwebtoken\';\\nimport type { Request, Response, NextFunction } from \'express\';\\nimport { db } from \'./db.ts\';\\n\\nconst JWT_SECRET = process.env.JWT_SECRET || \'movex-hackathon-dev-secret-2026\';\\n\\nexport interface AuthUser {\\n  id: number;\\n  name: string;\\n  email: string;\\n  mobile: string;\\n  role: \'sender\' | \'partner\' | \'admin\';\\n  can_deliver: number;\\n  verification_status: \'VERIFIED\' | \'PENDING\' | \'SUSPENDED\';\\n  rating: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface AuthedRequest extends Request {\\n  user?: AuthUser;\\n}\\n\\nexport function signToken(user: AuthUser): string {\\n  return jwt.sign(\\n    { sub: user.id, email: user.email, role: user.role },\\n    JWT_SECRET,\\n    { expiresIn: \'7d\' }\\n  );\\n}\\n\\nexport function validatePasswordStrength(password: string): string | null {\\n  if (!password || password.length < 8) {\\n    return \'Password must be at least 8 characters long.\';\\n  }\\n  if (!/[A-Za-z]/.test(password) || !/[0-9]/.test(password)) {\\n    return \'Password must include at least one letter and one number.\';\\n  }\\n  return null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function requireAuth(req: AuthedRequest, res: Response, next: NextFunction) {\\n  const header = req.headers.authorization || \'\';\\n  const token = header.startsWith(\'Bearer \') ? header.slice(7) : \'\';\\n  if (!token) {\\n    res.status(401).json({ error: \'Authentication required. Please log in.\' });\\n    return;\\n  }\\n\\n  try {\\n    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET) as { sub: number };\\n    const user = db.prepare(\\n      \'SELECT id, name, email, mobile, role, can_deliver, verification_status, rating FROM users WHERE id = ?\'\\n    ).get(decoded.sub) as AuthUser | undefined;\\n\\n    if (!user) {\\n      res.status(401).json({ error: \'Account not found.\' });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (user.verification_status === \'SUSPENDED\') {\\n      res.status(403).json({ error: \'Account is currently suspended. Contact MOVEX support.\' });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\\n    req.user = user;\\n    next();\\n  } catch {\\n    res.status(401).json({ error: \'Invalid or expired session token. Please log in again.\' });\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function optionalAuth(req: AuthedRequest, _res: Response, next: NextFunction) {\\n  const header = req.headers.authorization || \'\';\\n  const token = header.startsWith(\'Bearer \') ? header.slice(7) : \'\';\\n  if (!token) {\\n    next();\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  try {\\n    const decoded = jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET) as { sub: number };\\n    const user = db.prepare(\\n      \'SELECT id, name, email, mobile, role, can_deliver, verification_status, rating FROM users WHERE id = ?\'\\n    ).get(decoded.sub) as AuthUser | undefined;\\n    if (user && user.verification_status !== \'SUSPENDED\') {\\n      req.user = user;\\n    }\\n  } catch {\\n    // ignore invalid optional token\\n  }\\n  next();\\n}\\n\\nexport function requireRole(...roles: Array<\'sender\' | \'partner\' | \'admin\'>) {\\n  return (req: AuthedRequest, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\\n    if (!req.user) {\\n      res.status(401).json({ error: \'Authentication required.\' });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!roles.includes(req.user.role)) {\\n      res.status(403).json({ error: \'Access denied for your account role.\' });\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    next();\\n  };\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Create JWT authentication, password validation, and role-based access middleware in server/auth.ts\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/server/auth.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating JWT authentication middleware\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create JWT auth middleware\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\363A\n\360A\001i\024}\023\324\222\2210\016\vDv\226)\255+_\035\337\337N\217s\242\247b\201\333\274\037h\033\030u+V\267\004\334J\024)2\264{5O\253\203W\241&\035\a\177-\355W\314\006\241\237\276\343\300\327-\314\344\03406\350\257K0\000l\217\312\315\217\275T\276 \250\341\t\324Y\257\005N\033C\031\372\372Sf\303\272\t-{7R\033#\016\331nUF.\365\314\374\212\255\234\337 G\'\234\213\210(\034\024%E]\262\312S)\305\230b\377}\337I\347wl\020\272\336\357\356\327\210\216\277\00118\340\260\240\346=yUtSX\376\312(\232\256\273\205\225}C\335I\f My;\360R\316|t\272\311`N\312\020\325\'\350\357\274\223B;_\270b\321=7\033\367\360pR\345\201}8C\255\255\3000O%\247]\334\n\364\035\330\\\223\223\366X\213\024]_\376\260\353\031\274\265\313JA%\340\251\"\373+\322)<x\035E4j\307\330X,\\\207\212\244\353\352\263TXl\346J\253\276\2229\316\371\nn\327\373\377h*\005\fS\2674Z\333~\262\b~)\005\353<&\021E`\024c\225|\213\345\243s\271\t}\nLH\025\331\264Q\361!\252v.\306M\266\017\336\207\347\270+J\227\212\376d\277~(1eb\220XO\2771Ym\376|>\345\316\036\226J\201\346\337O\356\323\350jK\221\217\312cm\005\355.zQ\346V\205\335\a^M\350\243\271K\323\312\263G\a\251\226\333\001{*\237\036\253\230@\372\334\203x\276\342[\313\276\347#\301\001g\304\253\210\331\373\236\362\271)\177\263\236\314\v\200\r\301\313\235\326\254\001WH\376\307\257 rP\276\3359\341\245\241\027\032\003<\366W\022&\245\na\231\215VH\377\252\264\001U>\2123MiFeP\367:\230*\213\vO\0374;\264\022-{<\351\255$\356\251]B\351\334\232y\367\242\364\243\023-53~\234\211y\230\177/\306\341\355\231%\214<\212.E\314@\272Zq\n\251\333\262K#\316\216\331\261\204#\002\216\t\000h#.\375}+k\027[\320O.\320\r:T\207e\373\307\373D6\357w\373\3513;1!\354\342\227\214\016\v\346}\226(\242\315d\207\343\362\251\340\245\344h\373\tGJ\275\\\230\240\355\266\025\023\352\220\242\347\246\252??\320\2649\356]\024!\201:\215G\236\256\304#\255\232\265\3605\333g\215\210&\240\021\312`x>\035\264\363\364\205\016\250\031\334\205\263;uw7s\3068y@};x\346B\206\330\310L\372\340\376\"({E\254\a\333\0065